# A test that several kinds of value pass tries its cases one after the other: only the last one can fail the test, and a number that needs a test of its own is decided in its own arm. However many cases can fail, a failed test throws nothing: the function has no site, and its only call is the one that asks whether a cell is callable
# FORM: Selected
# RUN: generate-code calls
# OPTIONS: heat=everything-is-hot check=validate-back-end

module m0 path="main.js" displayPath="main.js"
function f0 name="numberOrNothing" parameters=[{type=anything}] results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0(v0: anything):
    v1 = TypeTest v0 testedType=undefined|null|number
    TestAndBranch v1 -> taken b1(| 0), notTaken b2(| 0)
  b1(v2):
    Return v2
  b2(v3) frequency=Unlikely:
    Return v3
}
# CHECK: f0: size={{*}} sites=0 handlers
# CHECK-NOT: operation
# CHECK-NOT: ThrowAtSite
function f1 name="booleanNumberOrNothing" parameters=[{type=anything}] results=[{type=anything}] {
